{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>With whom did He consult.</b> From the nifal binyan, past tense; therefore it has patach under the ayin — with whom did He take counsel." "<b>And made Him understand.</b> And gave understanding to the Name, and taught Him the path of justice, that the Name is for every discipline and instruction." "<b>And taught Him knowledge.</b> The futures."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:06.951384183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}